1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,599
It is Friday afternoon. Someone pushes code. And nobody knows if it still builds.

2
00:00:06,149 --> 00:00:07,682
Somebody has to build it,

3
00:00:07,682 --> 00:00:08,173
test it,

4
00:00:08,173 --> 00:00:09,277
and tell the team.

5
00:00:09,277 --> 00:00:10,442
Doing that by hand,

6
00:00:10,442 --> 00:00:11,117
every time,

7
00:00:11,117 --> 00:00:12,037
does not scale.

8
00:00:12,587 --> 00:00:14,082
Jenkins does it for you.

9
00:00:14,082 --> 00:00:16,450
It is a server that watches your code,

10
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:17,073
builds it,

11
00:00:17,073 --> 00:00:17,634
tests it,

12
00:00:17,634 --> 00:00:19,691
and shows the result on one page.

13
00:00:20,241 --> 00:00:21,795
Today you meet Jenkins.

14
00:00:21,795 --> 00:00:23,958
First the ideas: the controller,

15
00:00:23,958 --> 00:00:24,701
the agents,

16
00:00:24,701 --> 00:00:25,647
the executors,

17
00:00:25,647 --> 00:00:26,458
the plugins.

18
00:00:26,458 --> 00:00:27,810
Then the real thing,

19
00:00:27,810 --> 00:00:28,486
on screen,

20
00:00:28,486 --> 00:00:29,499
click by click.

21
00:00:31,049 --> 00:00:32,478
Here is what to expect.

22
00:00:33,028 --> 00:00:36,826
One: the architecture. What a controller is, and what an agent is.

23
00:00:37,376 --> 00:00:42,026
Two: executors, and the queue. How Jenkins decides who builds what, and when.

24
00:00:42,576 --> 00:00:46,544
Three: plugins, and the life of a build, from the trigger to the result.

25
00:00:47,094 --> 00:00:49,447
Four: a live tour of a real Jenkins.

26
00:00:49,447 --> 00:00:51,081
Every part of the screen,

27
00:00:51,081 --> 00:00:51,473
named.

28
00:00:51,473 --> 00:00:52,780
Then your first job,

29
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:53,303
a queue,

30
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:54,284
and a pipeline.

31
00:00:54,834 --> 00:00:57,394
This is objective one of the Jenkins domain.

32
00:00:59,444 --> 00:01:00,553
The architecture.

33
00:01:01,103 --> 00:01:03,023
The controller is the brain.

34
00:01:03,023 --> 00:01:05,012
It is the one Jenkins server.

35
00:01:05,012 --> 00:01:06,520
It shows the web page,

36
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:08,852
stores every job and every result,

37
00:01:08,852 --> 00:01:10,703
and decides what runs next.

38
00:01:11,253 --> 00:01:13,898
An agent is a machine that does the work.

39
00:01:13,898 --> 00:01:15,962
The controller sends it a build,

40
00:01:15,962 --> 00:01:17,123
the agent runs it,

41
00:01:17,123 --> 00:01:18,800
and sends the result back.

42
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:20,219
Agents can be servers,

43
00:01:20,219 --> 00:01:20,929
containers,

44
00:01:20,929 --> 00:01:22,219
or virtual machines.

45
00:01:22,769 --> 00:01:25,106
Our first lab has only one machine.

46
00:01:25,106 --> 00:01:27,443
Jenkins calls it the built in node,

47
00:01:27,443 --> 00:01:30,515
which is the controller running builds itself.

48
00:01:30,515 --> 00:01:32,251
That is fine for learning.

49
00:01:32,251 --> 00:01:33,186
In real teams,

50
00:01:33,186 --> 00:01:34,588
builds run on agents,

51
00:01:34,588 --> 00:01:37,126
so the controller stays free and safe.

52
00:01:37,676 --> 00:01:40,293
An executor is one slot to run one build.

53
00:01:40,293 --> 00:01:44,251
A machine with two executors runs two builds at the same time.

54
00:01:44,251 --> 00:01:46,039
The third build has to wait.

55
00:01:46,589 --> 00:01:48,957
Where does the waiting happen? In the build queue.

56
00:01:49,507 --> 00:01:53,993
And everything Jenkins knows lives in one folder on the controller.

57
00:01:53,993 --> 00:01:55,734
It is called Jenkins home.

58
00:01:55,734 --> 00:01:56,069
Jobs,

59
00:01:56,069 --> 00:01:56,672
settings,

60
00:01:56,672 --> 00:01:57,207
plugins,

61
00:01:57,207 --> 00:01:58,145
build history.

62
00:01:58,145 --> 00:01:59,484
Back up that folder,

63
00:01:59,484 --> 00:02:01,560
and you have backed up Jenkins.

64
00:02:03,110 --> 00:02:04,305
The life of a build.

65
00:02:04,855 --> 00:02:05,887
One: a trigger.

66
00:02:05,887 --> 00:02:07,676
A person clicks Build Now,

67
00:02:07,676 --> 00:02:08,708
or a code push,

68
00:02:08,708 --> 00:02:09,465
or a timer,

69
00:02:09,465 --> 00:02:11,255
asks Jenkins to run a job.

70
00:02:11,805 --> 00:02:16,114
Two: the build joins the queue. It waits for a free executor that matches.

71
00:02:16,664 --> 00:02:18,517
Three: an executor takes it.

72
00:02:18,517 --> 00:02:20,238
Jenkins makes a workspace,

73
00:02:20,238 --> 00:02:22,289
a clean folder on that machine,

74
00:02:22,289 --> 00:02:23,149
for this job.

75
00:02:23,699 --> 00:02:25,061
Four: the steps run.

76
00:02:25,061 --> 00:02:26,083
Shell commands,

77
00:02:26,083 --> 00:02:27,309
one after another,

78
00:02:27,309 --> 00:02:29,216
or the stages of a pipeline.

79
00:02:29,216 --> 00:02:31,259
Every line of output is saved,

80
00:02:31,259 --> 00:02:32,553
as the console log.

81
00:02:33,103 --> 00:02:34,257
Five: the result.

82
00:02:34,257 --> 00:02:36,023
Blue or green for success,

83
00:02:36,023 --> 00:02:37,110
red for failure,

84
00:02:37,110 --> 00:02:38,536
and grey for aborted.

85
00:02:38,536 --> 00:02:41,321
Then optional follow up work: save files,

86
00:02:41,321 --> 00:02:42,340
send a message.

87
00:02:42,890 --> 00:02:45,676
And plugins add almost everything else.

88
00:02:45,676 --> 00:02:45,962
Git,

89
00:02:45,962 --> 00:02:46,676
pipelines,

90
00:02:46,676 --> 00:02:47,534
credentials,

91
00:02:47,534 --> 00:02:47,962
email.

92
00:02:47,962 --> 00:02:49,534
Jenkins core is small.

93
00:02:49,534 --> 00:02:50,963
Plugins make it big.

94
00:02:50,963 --> 00:02:52,177
So keep them few,

95
00:02:52,177 --> 00:02:53,749
and keep them updated.

96
00:02:55,299 --> 00:02:56,595
Now the real thing.

97
00:02:56,595 --> 00:02:59,939
This is a continuous recording of a real Jenkins,

98
00:02:59,939 --> 00:03:01,986
version 2.580,

99
00:03:01,986 --> 00:03:03,214
long term support,

100
00:03:03,214 --> 00:03:04,238
on one machine.

101
00:03:04,788 --> 00:03:05,720
I open Chrome,

102
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:07,051
and type localhost

103
00:03:07,051 --> 00:03:08,382
colon 8080.

104
00:03:08,382 --> 00:03:09,847
Jenkins asks who I am.

105
00:03:09,847 --> 00:03:11,245
I type the user name,

106
00:03:11,245 --> 00:03:12,443
then the password,

107
00:03:12,443 --> 00:03:13,641
and press Sign in.

108
00:03:14,191 --> 00:03:15,602
This is the dashboard.

109
00:03:15,602 --> 00:03:16,949
Four regions to know.

110
00:03:16,949 --> 00:03:17,655
At the top,

111
00:03:17,655 --> 00:03:19,515
the header: the Jenkins logo,

112
00:03:19,515 --> 00:03:20,349
a search box,

113
00:03:20,349 --> 00:03:22,595
the gear that opens Manage Jenkins,

114
00:03:22,595 --> 00:03:23,878
and my account menu.

115
00:03:23,878 --> 00:03:24,647
On the left,

116
00:03:24,647 --> 00:03:25,545
the main menu,

117
00:03:25,545 --> 00:03:28,560
with two small boxes below it: the build queue,

118
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:30,485
and the build executor status.

119
00:03:30,485 --> 00:03:31,640
And in the middle,

120
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:32,538
the main area.

121
00:03:33,088 --> 00:03:34,681
The main menu is short.

122
00:03:34,681 --> 00:03:36,274
New Item creates a job.

123
00:03:36,274 --> 00:03:38,491
Build History shows every build,

124
00:03:38,491 --> 00:03:39,530
from every job.

125
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:42,163
The gear at the top is Manage Jenkins,

126
00:03:42,163 --> 00:03:43,341
the control room.

127
00:03:43,341 --> 00:03:46,250
And my account menu holds my own settings.

128
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:49,343
The main area says Welcome to Jenkins,

129
00:03:49,343 --> 00:03:51,350
because there are no jobs yet.

130
00:03:51,350 --> 00:03:53,156
Later this becomes a table,

131
00:03:53,156 --> 00:03:54,227
one row per job,

132
00:03:54,227 --> 00:03:56,702
with its status and its latest build.

133
00:03:56,702 --> 00:03:57,237
For now,

134
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:59,780
it offers two shortcuts: create a job,

135
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:01,051
or set up an agent.

136
00:04:01,601 --> 00:04:03,301
Now the executor status.

137
00:04:03,301 --> 00:04:06,419
It says zero slash two: zero builds running,

138
00:04:06,419 --> 00:04:08,261
out of two executor slots.

139
00:04:08,261 --> 00:04:09,324
Two free slots,

140
00:04:09,324 --> 00:04:10,387
ready for work.

141
00:04:10,387 --> 00:04:11,662
Remember this box.

142
00:04:11,662 --> 00:04:13,292
It matters in a minute.

143
00:04:13,842 --> 00:04:15,064
Now Manage Jenkins,

144
00:04:15,064 --> 00:04:16,158
the control room.

145
00:04:16,158 --> 00:04:16,866
At the top,

146
00:04:16,866 --> 00:04:18,346
Jenkins shows warnings.

147
00:04:18,346 --> 00:04:22,786
This one says: building on the built in node can be a security issue.

148
00:04:22,786 --> 00:04:25,038
A good habit is to build on agents.

149
00:04:25,038 --> 00:04:26,389
Below are the groups.

150
00:04:26,389 --> 00:04:28,835
System Configuration: system settings,

151
00:04:28,835 --> 00:04:29,221
tools,

152
00:04:29,221 --> 00:04:29,736
plugins,

153
00:04:29,736 --> 00:04:30,379
and nodes.

154
00:04:30,379 --> 00:04:31,280
Then Security,

155
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:33,017
with users and credentials.

156
00:04:33,017 --> 00:04:34,562
Then Status Information,

157
00:04:34,562 --> 00:04:35,849
and Troubleshooting,

158
00:04:35,849 --> 00:04:37,522
for when something breaks.

159
00:04:38,072 --> 00:04:38,837
Nodes first.

160
00:04:38,837 --> 00:04:40,494
Here is the built in node,

161
00:04:40,494 --> 00:04:41,896
the controller itself.

162
00:04:41,896 --> 00:04:42,980
Its architecture,

163
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:44,255
its free disk space,

164
00:04:44,255 --> 00:04:45,657
and its response time.

165
00:04:45,657 --> 00:04:46,805
In a later lesson,

166
00:04:46,805 --> 00:04:48,717
this is where we add an agent.

167
00:04:49,267 --> 00:04:49,841
Plugins,

168
00:04:49,841 --> 00:04:51,779
and then Installed plugins.

169
00:04:51,779 --> 00:04:53,717
Jenkins already has dozens.

170
00:04:53,717 --> 00:04:56,157
In the search box I type pipeline,

171
00:04:56,157 --> 00:04:58,454
and the pipeline plugins appear.

172
00:04:58,454 --> 00:05:00,248
Each plugin is a feature.

173
00:05:00,248 --> 00:05:00,536
Git,

174
00:05:00,536 --> 00:05:01,397
credentials,

175
00:05:01,397 --> 00:05:02,186
timestamps,

176
00:05:02,186 --> 00:05:02,617
email.

177
00:05:02,617 --> 00:05:06,206
Remember: more plugins means more to keep updated.

178
00:05:06,756 --> 00:05:07,984
Now the first job.

179
00:05:07,984 --> 00:05:09,145
I click New Item.

180
00:05:09,145 --> 00:05:11,534
I give it a name: hello controller.

181
00:05:11,534 --> 00:05:13,104
Then I choose the type.

182
00:05:13,104 --> 00:05:16,859
Freestyle project is the simplest one: a list of steps.

183
00:05:16,859 --> 00:05:18,702
Pipeline is the modern one,

184
00:05:18,702 --> 00:05:19,248
as code,

185
00:05:19,248 --> 00:05:20,887
and we will use it soon.

186
00:05:20,887 --> 00:05:22,184
I choose Freestyle,

187
00:05:22,184 --> 00:05:23,140
and click O K.

188
00:05:23,690 --> 00:05:25,254
The configuration page.

189
00:05:25,254 --> 00:05:28,587
The menu on the left lists the sections: General,

190
00:05:28,587 --> 00:05:30,152
Source Code Management,

191
00:05:30,152 --> 00:05:30,764
Triggers,

192
00:05:30,764 --> 00:05:31,581
Environment,

193
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:32,397
Build Steps,

194
00:05:32,397 --> 00:05:33,961
and Post build actions.

195
00:05:33,961 --> 00:05:36,614
A job can start from a code repository,

196
00:05:36,614 --> 00:05:37,771
run on a trigger,

197
00:05:37,771 --> 00:05:39,676
and do work after the build.

198
00:05:39,676 --> 00:05:41,716
Today I only need one section.

199
00:05:42,266 --> 00:05:43,073
Build Steps.

200
00:05:43,073 --> 00:05:44,081
Add build step,

201
00:05:44,081 --> 00:05:45,761
and choose Execute shell.

202
00:05:45,761 --> 00:05:48,046
I type three small commands: echo,

203
00:05:48,046 --> 00:05:49,122
a hello message.

204
00:05:49,122 --> 00:05:50,063
Then hostname,

205
00:05:50,063 --> 00:05:52,079
which prints the machine name.

206
00:05:52,079 --> 00:05:52,953
And who am I,

207
00:05:52,953 --> 00:05:55,776
which prints the user that runs the build.

208
00:05:55,776 --> 00:05:56,112
Save.

209
00:05:56,662 --> 00:05:57,579
The job page.

210
00:05:57,579 --> 00:05:58,989
On the left: Status,

211
00:05:58,989 --> 00:05:59,554
Changes,

212
00:05:59,554 --> 00:06:00,259
Workspace,

213
00:06:00,259 --> 00:06:00,964
Build Now,

214
00:06:00,964 --> 00:06:01,952
and Configure.

215
00:06:01,952 --> 00:06:03,715
Build Now starts a build.

216
00:06:03,715 --> 00:06:04,491
I click it.

217
00:06:05,041 --> 00:06:07,393
A build appears in the Builds list.

218
00:06:07,393 --> 00:06:08,132
Number one.

219
00:06:08,132 --> 00:06:09,677
The icon is the status.

220
00:06:09,677 --> 00:06:10,685
First it spins,

221
00:06:10,685 --> 00:06:12,096
while the build runs.

222
00:06:12,096 --> 00:06:13,709
Now it is a green check.

223
00:06:13,709 --> 00:06:15,053
Green means success.

224
00:06:15,053 --> 00:06:16,262
Red means failure.

225
00:06:16,812 --> 00:06:17,858
Click build one.

226
00:06:17,858 --> 00:06:19,100
And Console Output.

227
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:20,472
This is the full log.

228
00:06:20,472 --> 00:06:21,910
Started by user admin.

229
00:06:21,910 --> 00:06:23,086
Running as system,

230
00:06:23,086 --> 00:06:24,197
in the workspace.

231
00:06:24,197 --> 00:06:25,700
Then my three commands,

232
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:26,811
and their output.

233
00:06:26,811 --> 00:06:27,922
The machine name.

234
00:06:27,922 --> 00:06:28,510
The user,

235
00:06:28,510 --> 00:06:29,621
which is Jenkins.

236
00:06:29,621 --> 00:06:31,451
And at the bottom: Finished,

237
00:06:31,451 --> 00:06:31,974
success.

238
00:06:31,974 --> 00:06:33,216
When a build fails,

239
00:06:33,216 --> 00:06:35,372
this is the first place you look.

240
00:06:35,922 --> 00:06:37,312
Back on the job page,

241
00:06:37,312 --> 00:06:37,974
Workspace.

242
00:06:37,974 --> 00:06:40,952
This is the folder Jenkins made for this job,

243
00:06:40,952 --> 00:06:42,872
on the machine that built it.

244
00:06:42,872 --> 00:06:43,534
Empty now,

245
00:06:43,534 --> 00:06:45,056
because we had no code.

246
00:06:45,056 --> 00:06:45,453
Later,

247
00:06:45,453 --> 00:06:46,909
our code will be here.

248
00:06:47,459 --> 00:06:48,401
Now the queue,

249
00:06:48,401 --> 00:06:49,613
and the executors.

250
00:06:49,613 --> 00:06:51,968
I prepared a job called slow build.

251
00:06:51,968 --> 00:06:54,459
It just waits for forty five seconds.

252
00:06:54,459 --> 00:06:55,670
I click Build Now,

253
00:06:55,670 --> 00:06:56,478
three times,

254
00:06:56,478 --> 00:06:57,016
quickly.

255
00:06:57,566 --> 00:06:59,077
Look at the bottom left.

256
00:06:59,077 --> 00:07:00,588
Both executors are busy.

257
00:07:00,588 --> 00:07:01,972
Slow build number one,

258
00:07:01,972 --> 00:07:02,917
and number two.

259
00:07:02,917 --> 00:07:05,497
The third build waits in the build queue.

260
00:07:05,497 --> 00:07:07,134
When an executor finishes,

261
00:07:07,134 --> 00:07:08,141
the queue moves.

262
00:07:08,141 --> 00:07:10,281
That is the whole scheduling idea.

263
00:07:10,831 --> 00:07:11,903
Now a pipeline.

264
00:07:11,903 --> 00:07:14,331
This one is called hello pipeline.

265
00:07:14,331 --> 00:07:15,260
In Configure,

266
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:17,975
the Pipeline section holds the script.

267
00:07:17,975 --> 00:07:20,904
A pipeline is a recipe in code: an agent,

268
00:07:20,904 --> 00:07:22,118
and three stages.

269
00:07:22,118 --> 00:07:22,547
Build,

270
00:07:22,547 --> 00:07:22,904
test,

271
00:07:22,904 --> 00:07:23,690
and deploy.

272
00:07:23,690 --> 00:07:25,190
Each stage has steps.

273
00:07:25,190 --> 00:07:26,833
This is a Jenkinsfile.

274
00:07:26,833 --> 00:07:28,262
In the next lessons,

275
00:07:28,262 --> 00:07:29,476
we write our own.

276
00:07:30,026 --> 00:07:30,715
Build Now.

277
00:07:30,715 --> 00:07:32,229
Then I open the build,

278
00:07:32,229 --> 00:07:34,018
and its pipeline overview.

279
00:07:34,018 --> 00:07:36,702
The stages are drawn as a graph: Build,

280
00:07:36,702 --> 00:07:37,046
Test,

281
00:07:37,046 --> 00:07:37,528
Deploy.

282
00:07:37,528 --> 00:07:40,005
Each circle fills as its stage runs,

283
00:07:40,005 --> 00:07:42,620
and turns green when the stage passes.

284
00:07:42,620 --> 00:07:44,891
A pipeline shows you where it is.

285
00:07:44,891 --> 00:07:46,474
A freestyle job cannot.

286
00:07:47,024 --> 00:07:47,541
Finally,

287
00:07:47,541 --> 00:07:48,186
a failure,

288
00:07:48,186 --> 00:07:48,897
on purpose.

289
00:07:48,897 --> 00:07:49,930
Broken pipeline.

290
00:07:49,930 --> 00:07:50,640
I build it,

291
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:52,060
and open the overview.

292
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:54,062
The Test stage has a red cross.

293
00:07:54,062 --> 00:07:55,934
Deploy is grey: it never ran,

294
00:07:55,934 --> 00:07:58,646
because a failed stage stops the pipeline.

295
00:07:58,646 --> 00:07:59,485
I click Test,

296
00:07:59,485 --> 00:08:01,486
and the log opens on the right.

297
00:08:01,486 --> 00:08:04,004
Here is the error: expected five items,

298
00:08:04,004 --> 00:08:04,715
found four.

299
00:08:04,715 --> 00:08:07,878
And the last line: script returned exit code one.

300
00:08:07,878 --> 00:08:09,557
Read the last lines first.

301
00:08:09,557 --> 00:08:11,494
That is how you debug a build.

302
00:08:12,044 --> 00:08:17,462
That is Jenkins. A controller, a queue, executors, and a clear page for every result.

303
00:08:19,012 --> 00:08:21,807
